    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0384" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123.G35/41.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister of
                        Cuba</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 57.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 28, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department is in receipt of a telegram
                    from the American Chargé d’Affaires at Habana stating that while entering the
                    Miramar Hotel on the evening of August 27 he was assaulted from behind, without
                    provocation or warning, by a reporter of La Prensa <pb facs="0385" n="269"
                        xml:id="pg269"/> who had been excluded from the Legation and from the
                    Department of State of Cuba because of false statements and who is said to be
                    notorious as having figured in many unsavory incidents. Mr. Gibson was knocked
                    senseless and while in this condition an attempt was made by the assailant to
                    inflict further injuries.</p>
                <p>This Department expects the Cuban Government to take prompt and energetic
                    measures adequately to punish the offender.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
